    "participation": "The labor force consists of employed and unemployed people. Each participation rate divides the labor force of the selected group by its population aged 15 and older.",
    "unemployment": "Unemployed people are without work, available for work and seeking employment. The published rate uses the labor force of the selected group as its denominator.",
    "groups": "Total, female and male are separate series. Each total rate is retained directly from the publisher.",
    "interpretation": "To express the unemployed as a percentage of the population aged 15 and older, multiply the participation rate by the unemployment rate and divide by 100. This uses both estimates for the same economy, year and population group. Multiplying rounded publisher rates can introduce small differences from a separately published employment-to-population ratio. The ILO model combines reported and modeled observations; this release supplies no observation-level imputation flag."
  },
